Two declarations in the patient chart use `UserIcon`, both as the icon inside an "orderer information" tooltip. Both would be affected by a behaviour change.

1. **`InfoTooltip` in the orders app** (`packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/components/medication-record.component.tsx`, lines 105-117). It renders `<UserIcon size={16} />` at line 110 as the trigger of a Carbon `Toggletip`, and shows the orderer's name in the tooltip content. `MedicationRecord` renders it at line 27. The `UserIcon` import is at line 5. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/components/medication-record.component.tsx:105-117}

2. **`InfoTooltip` in the medications app** (`packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/components/medications-details-table.component.tsx`, lines 376-382). It renders `<UserIcon size={16} />` at line 379 inside an `IconButton` whose label is the orderer name. It is used by the medications details table. The `UserIcon` import is at line 48. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/components/medications-details-table.component.tsx:376-382}

The `UserIcon` definition lives in `openmrs-esm-core` at `packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/icons/icons.tsx:824`, with mocks in `esm-styleguide/mock.tsx:99` and `mock-jest.tsx:98`. Those mocks render a plain `<span>` with the text "UserIcon". A behaviour change would therefore also alter test output wherever these mocks are used, though the mocks are not patient chart code. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/icons/icons.tsx:824}

Scope: I searched only the patient chart repo for usages and `openmrs-esm-core` for the definition. Other repositories in the product could also use `UserIcon`, but the question asks about the patient chart app, so I did not search them. I also did not read the test files in the patient chart for assertions on the icon.

